WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.101 --> 00:00:08.910
In this video you’ll put a photo of your hand sketch, a site plan, or an aerial

2
00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:13.476
photo under your map, then trace over it so the map matches your real site.

3
00:00:13.931 --> 00:00:20.182
Start a new map at your site. This time pick Start blank, then Create blank map.

4
00:00:21.544 --> 00:00:26.257
Open the Layers tab and choose Upload site plan or aerial photo.

5
00:00:26.257 --> 00:00:29.424
A phone photo of a paper sketch works fine.

6
00:00:29.875 --> 00:00:35.440
The picture goes on its own layer and is locked, so it won’t move while you draw.

7
00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:37.363
Choose Fit to see all of it.

8
00:00:37.815 --> 00:00:41.959
Turn the opacity down if the picture is hard to draw over.

9
00:00:42.411 --> 00:00:46.632
Now go back to Add and choose Draw a row of spaces.

10
00:00:46.632 --> 00:00:50.357
Drag along the front of a row in your sketch.

11
00:00:50.357 --> 00:00:53.502
The app works out how many spaces fit.

12
00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:58.575
Check the number of spaces, give the row its letter, and create it.

13
00:01:00.409 --> 00:01:02.456
Do the same for the next row.

14
00:01:10.151 --> 00:01:19.151
Rows can sit at an angle too. Drag along the angled row, and the row turns to match.

15
00:01:19.603 --> 00:01:27.403
For a curved lane, search the library for curved, and add a curved driving lane.

16
00:01:27.857 --> 00:01:30.923
Drag its ends to the ends of the lane in your sketch.

17
00:01:38.177 --> 00:01:42.557
Then pull the two bend handles until the curve sits on the lane.

18
00:01:46.139 --> 00:01:51.980
When you’re done, hide the picture from the Layers tab to see your map on its own.

19
00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:53.974
Everything you traced stays.
